{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition identity is the application update boundary. A framework memo\ncaptures the current data and options; Charts rebuilds the scene when that\ndefinition changes or when the chart surface changes size."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nfunction RankingChart({ rows, metric, accent }: Props) {\n  const definition = useMemo(() => {\n    const ranked = rows\n      .map((row) => ({ label: row.label, value: row[metric] }))\n      .sort((left, right) => right.value - left.value)\n\n    return defineChart({\n      svgAnimation: { duration: 280, easing: 'ease-out' },\n      chart: ({ width }) => ({\n        marks: [\n          barX(ranked, {\n            x: 'value',\n            y: 'label',\n            fill: accent,\n          }),\n        ],\n        scales: {\n          x: {\n            scale: scaleLinear,\n            nice: true,\n            axis: { ticks: { count: width < 420 ? 4 : 7 } },\n          },\n          y: {\n            scale: () => scaleBand<string>().padding(0.1),\n          },\n        },\n      }),\n    })\n  }, [rows, metric, accent])\n\n  return <Chart definition={definition} ariaLabel=\"Revenue ranking\" />\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the framework's native equivalent: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computed"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMemo"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$derived"},{"type":"text","value":",\nAngular "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computed"},{"type":"text","value":", or Octane "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMemo"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"vanilla","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vanilla"}]},{"type":"code","value":"host.update({\n  ...options,\n  definition: createRankingDefinition(nextRows, nextMetric, nextAccent),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"stable-keys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable keys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in marks first use an explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":", then a unique "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"datum.id"},{"type":"text","value":", then a\nunique nested "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"datum.data.id"},{"type":"text","value":". Marks can also infer identity from semantic\npositional channels:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"barX(rows, {\n  x: 'value',\n  y: 'label',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"barX"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the unique "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":" value when rows have no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"barY"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":";\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineY"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaY"},{"type":"text","value":" use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"areaX"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":"; rects and cells use their x/y\ninterval tuple. Dots and text try x, then y, then their x/y tuple. Inference is\nscoped to each group and falls back to array position when a candidate is\nincomplete or duplicated. Development builds warn once for each affected mark\ninstance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" when the inferred value is not the entity's identity or can\nchange independently of it. Stable identity preserves surviving SVG elements,\nfocused points, and transition continuity."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lightweight-svg-tweening","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lightweight SVG tweening"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" or:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"duration"},{"type":"text","value":": milliseconds;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"easing"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linear"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ease"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ease-in"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ease-out"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ease-in-out"},{"type":"text","value":", or a\nfunction from normalized progress to normalized progress;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"respectReducedMotion"},{"type":"text","value":": defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resize"},{"type":"text","value":": defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":", so responsive relayout does not repeatedly\nrestart animation."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Numeric geometry and compatible path data interpolate. Entering and exiting\nnodes reconcile by key. If an update interrupts a transition, it begins from\nthe geometry currently painted on screen."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static SVG, server rendering, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChartScene"},{"type":"text","value":" do not include animation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this path when a small default-SVG tween is enough. It has no spring\nsolver, definition-local timing cascade, entrance choreography, or retained\nvelocity."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"optional-tween-and-spring-motion","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional tween and spring motion"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion()"},{"type":"text","value":" when animation quality is part of the chart contract:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { motion } from '@tanstack/charts/motion'\nimport { stagger } from '@tanstack/charts/motion/definition'\nimport { mountChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/renderer'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  motion: {\n    path: 'morph',\n    ...stagger({ each: 35, roles: 'line', by: 'series' }),\n  },\n  marks: [\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'actual',\n      key: 'id',\n    }),\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'forecast',\n      key: 'id',\n      motion: { transition: { type: 'spring', mass: 1.25 } },\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})\n\nconst host = mountChartRenderer(container, {\n  definition,\n  renderer: motion({\n    transition: { type: 'spring', stiffness: 170, damping: 18, mass: 1 },\n  }),\n  width: 640,\n  height: 360,\n  ariaLabel: 'Actual and forecast revenue',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each host has one animation owner. The default SVG renderer uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation"},{"type":"text","value":".\nWhen "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion()"},{"type":"text","value":" is the renderer, it ignores "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation"},{"type":"text","value":" and uses motion\ndeclarations from the definition. A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"},{"type":"text","value":" declaration configures the motion\nrenderer; it does not select it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion declarations can live on the chart, a mark, an axis, its ticks, tick\nlabels, or axis label. A callback can specialize "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enter"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exit"},{"type":"text","value":"\nby series or datum:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"barY(rows, {\n  x: 'month',\n  y: 'revenue',\n  key: 'id',\n  motion(context) {\n    if (context.phase === 'enter') {\n      return { delay: context.datumIndex * 35 }\n    }\n    if (context.datum?.status === 'forecast') {\n      return { transition: { type: 'tween', duration: 240 } }\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same-type partial transitions inherit omitted properties. Springs use physical\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stiffness"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"damping"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mass"},{"type":"text","value":"; duration is not a spring parameter. Rapid\nretargeting preserves the currently painted value and velocity. Keyed\ninteraction points move with the presentation geometry rather than jumping to\nthe next scene."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crosshair"},{"type":"text","value":" is also keyed focus presentation. With the motion renderer, its\nrules, bands, labels, and marker retain DOM identity and spring velocity while\nfocus retargets. Default SVG, Canvas, and native surfaces paint the same guide\nat its current target without importing the browser motion runtime."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stagger()"},{"type":"text","value":" contributes only a context-aware delay, so it composes with\ntransition and path fields through normal object spread. Spring updates always\nretarget immediately; an update delay is ignored so incoming momentum cannot\nfreeze. Use delays for spring enter/exit choreography or any tween phase."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The renderer grows entering Cartesian bars, lines, and areas from their\nsemantic baseline; grows radial paths from the polar center; sweeps arcs\nthrough their authored angle; staggers bar entrances; morphs compatible\nnumeric SVG geometry; and keeps removed keys painted through their exit\ntransition. Authored delay replaces automatic staggering for that target."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion()"},{"type":"text","value":" respects reduced motion and does not animate resize-only updates by\ndefault. It adopts server-rendered SVG without replaying entrance motion by\ndefault; pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initial: 'always'"},{"type":"text","value":" to replay entrance motion after hydration.\nStatic SVG and Canvas accept the same definitions but paint the final state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/motion.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motion reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the complete cascade,\ntypes, focus-state transitions, compatibility limits, and standalone spring\nsampler."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/themes-and-motion.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Themes and Motion examples"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for complete\ncards that separate keyed chart motion from controls, labels, and palette CSS."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For high-rate data:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep source history outside the chart if the product needs it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capture a bounded visible window or encoded representation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preserve keys for rows that survive the roll."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep viewport state controlled."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Coalesce upstream work when only the latest state matters."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a scrolling trace, keep enough overscan before the visible x-domain to\ncover the largest expected update batch, enable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clip"},{"type":"text","value":", and use a rolling path\ncontract:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const definition = defineChart({\n  motion: {\n    path: {\n      update: 'rolling',\n      x: 'shift',\n      y: 'reproject',\n      fallback: 'snap',\n    },\n    transition: { type: 'tween', duration: sampleInterval, easing: 'linear' },\n  },\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The keyed retained window moves as one affine path. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y: 'reproject'"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps that\nmotion valid while a continuous y-domain changes. A failed rolling invariant\nsnaps instead of occasionally becoming a different interpolation. Set\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback: 'morph'"},{"type":"text","value":" only when path interpolation is intentional. A valid update\nthat arrives during another roll composes from the transform currently painted\non screen."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"viewport.translate"},{"type":"text","value":" at zero on both the previous and target scene during\na rolling update. A nonzero transient viewport translation makes the rolling\ncontract fail and uses its configured fallback. Commit the viewport domain and\nreset the translation before applying the next live-data window. Keep plot\nmargins fixed and prefer linear segments so appending a sample cannot recompute\na visible curve tangent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The final definition passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"host.update"},{"type":"text","value":" is applied synchronously."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"react","text":"React","level":2},{"id":"vanilla","text":"Vanilla","level":2},{"id":"stable-keys","text":"Stable keys","level":2},{"id":"lightweight-svg-tweening","text":"Lightweight SVG tweening","level":2},{"id":"optional-tween-and-spring-motion","text":"Optional tween and spring motion","level":2},{"id":"streaming","text":"Streaming","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefinition identity is the application update boundary. A framework memo\ncaptures the current data and options; Charts rebuilds the scene when that\ndefinition changes or when the chart surface changes size.\n\n## React\n\n```tsx\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nfunction RankingChart({ rows, metric, accent }: Props) {\n  const definition = useMemo(() => {\n    const ranked = rows\n      .map((row) => ({ label: row.label, value: row[metric] }))\n      .sort((left, right) => right.value - left.value)\n\n    return defineChart({\n      svgAnimation: { duration: 280, easing: 'ease-out' },\n      chart: ({ width }) => ({\n        marks: [\n          barX(ranked, {\n            x: 'value',\n            y: 'label',\n            fill: accent,\n          }),\n        ],\n        scales: {\n          x: {\n            scale: scaleLinear,\n            nice: true,\n            axis: { ticks: { count: width < 420 ? 4 : 7 } },\n          },\n          y: {\n            scale: () => scaleBand<string>().padding(0.1),\n          },\n        },\n      }),\n    })\n  }, [rows, metric, accent])\n\n  return <Chart definition={definition} ariaLabel=\"Revenue ranking\" />\n}\n```\n\nUse the framework's native equivalent: `computed`, `createMemo`, `$derived`,\nAngular `computed`, or Octane `useMemo`.\n\n## Vanilla\n\n```ts\nhost.update({\n  ...options,\n  definition: createRankingDefinition(nextRows, nextMetric, nextAccent),\n})\n```\n\n## Stable keys\n\nBuilt-in marks first use an explicit `key`, then a unique `datum.id`, then a\nunique nested `datum.data.id`. Marks can also infer identity from semantic\npositional channels:\n\n```ts\nbarX(rows, {\n  x: 'value',\n  y: 'label',\n})\n```\n\nHere `barX` uses the unique `y` value when rows have no `id`. `barY` uses `x`;\n`lineY` and `areaY` use `x`; `areaX` uses `y`; rects and cells use their x/y\ninterval tuple. Dots and text try x, then y, then their x/y tuple. Inference is\nscoped to each group and falls back to array position when a candidate is\nincomplete or duplicated. Development builds warn once for each affected mark\ninstance.\n\nSupply `key` when the inferred value is not the entity's identity or can\nchange independently of it. Stable identity preserves surviving SVG elements,\nfocused points, and transition continuity.\n\n## Lightweight SVG tweening\n\n`svgAnimation` accepts `true` or:\n\n- `duration`: milliseconds;\n- `easing`: `linear`, `ease`, `ease-in`, `ease-out`, `ease-in-out`, or a\n  function from normalized progress to normalized progress;\n- `respectReducedMotion`: defaults to `true`;\n- `resize`: defaults to `false`, so responsive relayout does not repeatedly\n  restart animation.\n\nNumeric geometry and compatible path data interpolate. Entering and exiting\nnodes reconcile by key. If an update interrupts a transition, it begins from\nthe geometry currently painted on screen.\n\nStatic SVG, server rendering, and `createChartScene` do not include animation.\n\nUse this path when a small default-SVG tween is enough. It has no spring\nsolver, definition-local timing cascade, entrance choreography, or retained\nvelocity.\n\n## Optional tween and spring motion\n\nUse `motion()` when animation quality is part of the chart contract:\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { motion } from '@tanstack/charts/motion'\nimport { stagger } from '@tanstack/charts/motion/definition'\nimport { mountChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/renderer'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  motion: {\n    path: 'morph',\n    ...stagger({ each: 35, roles: 'line', by: 'series' }),\n  },\n  marks: [\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'actual',\n      key: 'id',\n    }),\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'forecast',\n      key: 'id',\n      motion: { transition: { type: 'spring', mass: 1.25 } },\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})\n\nconst host = mountChartRenderer(container, {\n  definition,\n  renderer: motion({\n    transition: { type: 'spring', stiffness: 170, damping: 18, mass: 1 },\n  }),\n  width: 640,\n  height: 360,\n  ariaLabel: 'Actual and forecast revenue',\n})\n```\n\nEach host has one animation owner. The default SVG renderer uses `svgAnimation`.\nWhen `motion()` is the renderer, it ignores `svgAnimation` and uses motion\ndeclarations from the definition. A `motion` declaration configures the motion\nrenderer; it does not select it.\n\nMotion declarations can live on the chart, a mark, an axis, its ticks, tick\nlabels, or axis label. A callback can specialize `enter`, `update`, and `exit`\nby series or datum:\n\n```ts\nbarY(rows, {\n  x: 'month',\n  y: 'revenue',\n  key: 'id',\n  motion(context) {\n    if (context.phase === 'enter') {\n      return { delay: context.datumIndex * 35 }\n    }\n    if (context.datum?.status === 'forecast') {\n      return { transition: { type: 'tween', duration: 240 } }\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\nSame-type partial transitions inherit omitted properties. Springs use physical\n`stiffness`, `damping`, and `mass`; duration is not a spring parameter. Rapid\nretargeting preserves the currently painted value and velocity. Keyed\ninteraction points move with the presentation geometry rather than jumping to\nthe next scene.\n\nA `crosshair` is also keyed focus presentation. With the motion renderer, its\nrules, bands, labels, and marker retain DOM identity and spring velocity while\nfocus retargets. Default SVG, Canvas, and native surfaces paint the same guide\nat its current target without importing the browser motion runtime.\n\n`stagger()` contributes only a context-aware delay, so it composes with\ntransition and path fields through normal object spread. Spring updates always\nretarget immediately; an update delay is ignored so incoming momentum cannot\nfreeze. Use delays for spring enter/exit choreography or any tween phase.\n\nThe renderer grows entering Cartesian bars, lines, and areas from their\nsemantic baseline; grows radial paths from the polar center; sweeps arcs\nthrough their authored angle; staggers bar entrances; morphs compatible\nnumeric SVG geometry; and keeps removed keys painted through their exit\ntransition. Authored delay replaces automatic staggering for that target.\n\n`motion()` respects reduced motion and does not animate resize-only updates by\ndefault. It adopts server-rendered SVG without replaying entrance motion by\ndefault; pass `initial: 'always'` to replay entrance motion after hydration.\nStatic SVG and Canvas accept the same definitions but paint the final state.\n\nSee the [Motion reference](../reference/motion.md) for the complete cascade,\ntypes, focus-state transitions, compatibility limits, and standalone spring\nsampler.\n\nSee [Themes and Motion examples](../examples/themes-and-motion.md) for complete\ncards that separate keyed chart motion from controls, labels, and palette CSS.\n\n## Streaming\n\nFor high-rate data:\n\n1. Keep source history outside the chart if the product needs it.\n2. Capture a bounded visible window or encoded representation.\n3. Preserve keys for rows that survive the roll.\n4. Keep viewport state controlled.\n5. Coalesce upstream work when only the latest state matters.\n\nFor a scrolling trace, keep enough overscan before the visible x-domain to\ncover the largest expected update batch, enable `clip`, and use a rolling path\ncontract:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  motion: {\n    path: {\n      update: 'rolling',\n      x: 'shift',\n      y: 'reproject',\n      fallback: 'snap',\n    },\n    transition: { type: 'tween', duration: sampleInterval, easing: 'linear' },\n  },\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe keyed retained window moves as one affine path. `y: 'reproject'` keeps that\nmotion valid while a continuous y-domain changes. A failed rolling invariant\nsnaps instead of occasionally becoming a different interpolation. Set\n`fallback: 'morph'` only when path interpolation is intentional. A valid update\nthat arrives during another roll composes from the transform currently painted\non screen.\n\nKeep `viewport.translate` at zero on both the previous and target scene during\na rolling update. A nonzero transient viewport translation makes the rolling\ncontract fail and uses its configured fallback. Commit the viewport domain and\nreset the translation before applying the next live-data window. Keep plot\nmargins fixed and prefer linear segments so appending a sample cannot recompute\na visible curve tangent.\n\nThe final definition passed to `host.update` is applied synchronously.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Dynamic Data and Animation\ndescription: Recreate memoized definitions when application values change and animate keyed geometry safely.\n---\n\nDefinition identity is the application update boundary. A framework memo\ncaptures the current data and options; Charts rebuilds the scene when that\ndefinition changes or when the chart surface changes size.\n\n## React\n\n```tsx\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nfunction RankingChart({ rows, metric, accent }: Props) {\n  const definition = useMemo(() => {\n    const ranked = rows\n      .map((row) => ({ label: row.label, value: row[metric] }))\n      .sort((left, right) => right.value - left.value)\n\n    return defineChart({\n      svgAnimation: { duration: 280, easing: 'ease-out' },\n      chart: ({ width }) => ({\n        marks: [\n          barX(ranked, {\n            x: 'value',\n            y: 'label',\n            fill: accent,\n          }),\n        ],\n        scales: {\n          x: {\n            scale: scaleLinear,\n            nice: true,\n            axis: { ticks: { count: width < 420 ? 4 : 7 } },\n          },\n          y: {\n            scale: () => scaleBand<string>().padding(0.1),\n          },\n        },\n      }),\n    })\n  }, [rows, metric, accent])\n\n  return <Chart definition={definition} ariaLabel=\"Revenue ranking\" />\n}\n```\n\nUse the framework's native equivalent: `computed`, `createMemo`, `$derived`,\nAngular `computed`, or Octane `useMemo`.\n\n## Vanilla\n\n```ts\nhost.update({\n  ...options,\n  definition: createRankingDefinition(nextRows, nextMetric, nextAccent),\n})\n```\n\n## Stable keys\n\nBuilt-in marks first use an explicit `key`, then a unique `datum.id`, then a\nunique nested `datum.data.id`. Marks can also infer identity from semantic\npositional channels:\n\n```ts\nbarX(rows, {\n  x: 'value',\n  y: 'label',\n})\n```\n\nHere `barX` uses the unique `y` value when rows have no `id`. `barY` uses `x`;\n`lineY` and `areaY` use `x`; `areaX` uses `y`; rects and cells use their x/y\ninterval tuple. Dots and text try x, then y, then their x/y tuple. Inference is\nscoped to each group and falls back to array position when a candidate is\nincomplete or duplicated. Development builds warn once for each affected mark\ninstance.\n\nSupply `key` when the inferred value is not the entity's identity or can\nchange independently of it. Stable identity preserves surviving SVG elements,\nfocused points, and transition continuity.\n\n## Lightweight SVG tweening\n\n`svgAnimation` accepts `true` or:\n\n- `duration`: milliseconds;\n- `easing`: `linear`, `ease`, `ease-in`, `ease-out`, `ease-in-out`, or a\n  function from normalized progress to normalized progress;\n- `respectReducedMotion`: defaults to `true`;\n- `resize`: defaults to `false`, so responsive relayout does not repeatedly\n  restart animation.\n\nNumeric geometry and compatible path data interpolate. Entering and exiting\nnodes reconcile by key. If an update interrupts a transition, it begins from\nthe geometry currently painted on screen.\n\nStatic SVG, server rendering, and `createChartScene` do not include animation.\n\nUse this path when a small default-SVG tween is enough. It has no spring\nsolver, definition-local timing cascade, entrance choreography, or retained\nvelocity.\n\n## Optional tween and spring motion\n\nUse `motion()` when animation quality is part of the chart contract:\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { motion } from '@tanstack/charts/motion'\nimport { stagger } from '@tanstack/charts/motion/definition'\nimport { mountChartRenderer } from '@tanstack/charts/renderer'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  motion: {\n    path: 'morph',\n    ...stagger({ each: 35, roles: 'line', by: 'series' }),\n  },\n  marks: [\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'actual',\n      key: 'id',\n    }),\n    lineY(rows, {\n      x: 'date',\n      y: 'forecast',\n      key: 'id',\n      motion: { transition: { type: 'spring', mass: 1.25 } },\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear },\n  },\n})\n\nconst host = mountChartRenderer(container, {\n  definition,\n  renderer: motion({\n    transition: { type: 'spring', stiffness: 170, damping: 18, mass: 1 },\n  }),\n  width: 640,\n  height: 360,\n  ariaLabel: 'Actual and forecast revenue',\n})\n```\n\nEach host has one animation owner. The default SVG renderer uses `svgAnimation`.\nWhen `motion()` is the renderer, it ignores `svgAnimation` and uses motion\ndeclarations from the definition. A `motion` declaration configures the motion\nrenderer; it does not select it.\n\nMotion declarations can live on the chart, a mark, an axis, its ticks, tick\nlabels, or axis label. A callback can specialize `enter`, `update`, and `exit`\nby series or datum:\n\n```ts\nbarY(rows, {\n  x: 'month',\n  y: 'revenue',\n  key: 'id',\n  motion(context) {\n    if (context.phase === 'enter') {\n      return { delay: context.datumIndex * 35 }\n    }\n    if (context.datum?.status === 'forecast') {\n      return { transition: { type: 'tween', duration: 240 } }\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\nSame-type partial transitions inherit omitted properties. Springs use physical\n`stiffness`, `damping`, and `mass`; duration is not a spring parameter. Rapid\nretargeting preserves the currently painted value and velocity. Keyed\ninteraction points move with the presentation geometry rather than jumping to\nthe next scene.\n\nA `crosshair` is also keyed focus presentation. With the motion renderer, its\nrules, bands, labels, and marker retain DOM identity and spring velocity while\nfocus retargets. Default SVG, Canvas, and native surfaces paint the same guide\nat its current target without importing the browser motion runtime.\n\n`stagger()` contributes only a context-aware delay, so it composes with\ntransition and path fields through normal object spread. Spring updates always\nretarget immediately; an update delay is ignored so incoming momentum cannot\nfreeze. Use delays for spring enter/exit choreography or any tween phase.\n\nThe renderer grows entering Cartesian bars, lines, and areas from their\nsemantic baseline; grows radial paths from the polar center; sweeps arcs\nthrough their authored angle; staggers bar entrances; morphs compatible\nnumeric SVG geometry; and keeps removed keys painted through their exit\ntransition. Authored delay replaces automatic staggering for that target.\n\n`motion()` respects reduced motion and does not animate resize-only updates by\ndefault. It adopts server-rendered SVG without replaying entrance motion by\ndefault; pass `initial: 'always'` to replay entrance motion after hydration.\nStatic SVG and Canvas accept the same definitions but paint the final state.\n\nSee the [Motion reference](../reference/motion.md) for the complete cascade,\ntypes, focus-state transitions, compatibility limits, and standalone spring\nsampler.\n\nSee [Themes and Motion examples](../examples/themes-and-motion.md) for complete\ncards that separate keyed chart motion from controls, labels, and palette CSS.\n\n## Streaming\n\nFor high-rate data:\n\n1. Keep source history outside the chart if the product needs it.\n2. Capture a bounded visible window or encoded representation.\n3. Preserve keys for rows that survive the roll.\n4. Keep viewport state controlled.\n5. Coalesce upstream work when only the latest state matters.\n\nFor a scrolling trace, keep enough overscan before the visible x-domain to\ncover the largest expected update batch, enable `clip`, and use a rolling path\ncontract:\n\n```ts\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  motion: {\n    path: {\n      update: 'rolling',\n      x: 'shift',\n      y: 'reproject',\n      fallback: 'snap',\n    },\n    transition: { type: 'tween', duration: sampleInterval, easing: 'linear' },\n  },\n  marks,\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe keyed retained window moves as one affine path. `y: 'reproject'` keeps that\nmotion valid while a continuous y-domain changes. A failed rolling invariant\nsnaps instead of occasionally becoming a different interpolation. Set\n`fallback: 'morph'` only when path interpolation is intentional. A valid update\nthat arrives during another roll composes from the transform currently painted\non screen.\n\nKeep `viewport.translate` at zero on both the previous and target scene during\na rolling update. A nonzero transient viewport translation makes the rolling\ncontract fail and uses its configured fallback. Commit the viewport domain and\nreset the translation before applying the next live-data window. Keep plot\nmargins fixed and prefer linear segments so appending a sample cannot recompute\na visible curve tangent.\n\nThe final definition passed to `host.update` is applied synchronously.\n"}
